  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "ECMA.CEILING follows CEILING's sign and zero rules, returning #NUM! for positive number and negative significance",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 build 20527, ECMA.CEILING(number, significance) uses CEILING's sign and zero rules rather than CEILING.PRECISE's: it returns 0 when number = 0 or significance = 0, returns #NUM! when number > 0 and significance < 0, and rounds negative numbers up toward zero when significance > 0 (using the same 15-significant-digit quotient rounding as CEILING). All 2,773 full-bank ECMA.CEILING rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence readings/excel-20527/bank2-answers-ecma.ceiling-scalar.json and bank2-answers-ecma.ceiling-more.json (Excel 16.0 build 20527); 2,773/2,773 full-bank rows match.",
